h the same soil and water grow poorly when crowded beneath a canopy. What resource is most limited?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Gravity","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.9.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Body heat","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.9.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Light"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"DNA","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.9.1"}]},{"id":"life.ecosystems.h.010","deckId":"life.ecosystems","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"Each feeding level uses energy for life tasks and releases heat. What explains the smaller energy supply above it?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Energy is created by predators","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.10.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"All food becomes new tissue","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.10.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Nutrients vanish permanently","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.10.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Energy is used and dispersed as heat"}]},{"id":"life.ecosystems.h.011","deckId":"life.ecosystems","level":"hard","type":"order","prompt":"Order these events in leaf-litter nutrient recycling.","answer":["step-0","step-1","step-2","step-3"],"options":[{"id":"step-0","text":"Leaves fall"},{"id":"step-1","text":"Decomposers break them down"},{"id":"step-2","text":"Nutrients enter soil"},{"id":"step-3","text":"Roots absorb nutrients"}]},{"id":"life.ecosystems.h.012","deckId":"life.ecosystems","level":"hard","type":"diagram","prompt":"A species occurs naturally on one island and nowhere else. Which term fits this evidence?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Abiotic","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.12.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Endemic"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Domesticated","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.12.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Invasive everywhere","misconception":"life.ecosystems.mixup.12.2"}]},{"id":"life.genetics.e.001","deckId":"life.genetics","level":"easy","type":