ocity per unit time called?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Distance only","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Density","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Acceleration"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.3.1"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.e.004","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What quantity is the shortest directed change in position?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Distance traveled","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Elapsed time","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Average speed","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Displacement"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.e.005","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What does the slope of a distance-time graph show?","answer":"choice-0","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Speed"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Temperature","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Energy unit","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.5.3"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.e.006","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What does a horizontal distance-time line mean?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"The object has infinite speed","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"The object is at rest"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"The object speeds up","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.6.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"The object moves faster each second","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.6.2"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.e.007","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"In ideal projectile motion, which force acts during flight?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":