on","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What is needed to say whether an object is moving?","answer":"Reference frame","accept":["reference frame","Reference frame"]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.001","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A jeepney travels 120 m in 20 s. Which quantity is found by dividing these values?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Displacement only","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.1.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Average speed"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Acceleration","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Net force","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.1.2"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.002","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A jeepney travels at 10 m/s east. Which quantity does this statement give?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Speed alone","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.2.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Elapsed time","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Velocity"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.2.1"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.003","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A jeepney changes from 2 m/s to 8 m/s in 3 s. What type of quantity describes this change per second?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.3.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Distance only","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Density","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Acceleration"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.004","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A runner returns to the exact starting line after one lap. Which position-change quantity is zero?","answer":"choice-0","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Displacement"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Distance traveled","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Elapsed time","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Average speed","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.4.3"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.005","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A straight distance-time line becomes steeper. Which quantity has increased?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Energy unit","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.5.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Speed"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Temperature","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.5.2"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.006","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A cart’s recorded distance stays the same as time passes. What is happening?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"The object moves faster each second","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.6.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"The object has infinite speed","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"The object is at rest"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"The object speeds up","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.6.1"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.007","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A ball leaves a thrower’s hand. Ignore air resistance. Which force acts after release?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"A lasting hand push","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.7.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"No force at the top","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.7.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"A forward fuel force","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.7.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Gravity"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.m.008","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A thrown ball moves through air that offers no resistance in a model. What happens to its horizontal velocity?","answer":"choice-0","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":