2 m. Which motion quantity does that signed area represent?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Acceleration","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.10.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.10.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Force","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.10.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Displacement"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.h.011","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"hard","type":"order","prompt":"Order the height of a ball during its flight, from launch to landing.","answer":["step-0","step-1","step-2"],"options":[{"id":"step-0","text":"Ball rises"},{"id":"step-1","text":"Ball reaches its highest point"},{"id":"step-2","text":"Ball falls"}]},{"id":"physics.motion.h.012","deckId":"physics.motion","level":"hard","type":"diagram","prompt":"Two observers give different descriptions of the same passenger’s motion. Which choice explains the difference?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only eye color","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.12.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Reference frame"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Only body mass","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.12.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Only air temperature","misconception":"physics.motion.mixup.12.2"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.001","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What does sound need in order to travel?","answer":"choice-0","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"A material medium"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Empty space alone","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Light alone","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.1.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"No matter or energy","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.1.3"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.002","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"Which wave property mainly sets the pitch of a kulintang note?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only source size","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Frequency"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Only amplitude","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.2.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Only loudness","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.2.2"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.003","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"Which wave property is distance from rest to a crest?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Wavelength","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Period only","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Amplitude"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Frequency only","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.3.1"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.004","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the distance between adjacent wave crests called?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Amplitude","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Frequency","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.4.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Loudness","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Wavelength"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.005","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the number of complete wave cycles per second called?","answer":"choice-0","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Frequency"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Wavelength","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.5.1"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Amplitude","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Wave speed only","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.5.3"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.006","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"mcq","prompt":"Which formula links wave speed, frequency and wavelength?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"v = f + λ","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.6.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"v = f × λ"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"v = f / λ","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.6.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"v