ception":"physics.waves.mixup.10.2"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.011","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What SI unit is one wave cycle per second?","answer":"Hertz","accept":["hertz","Hertz"]},{"id":"physics.waves.e.012","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"easy","type":"input","prompt":"What do traveling waves transfer over long distances?","answer":"Energy","accept":["energy","Energy"]},{"id":"physics.waves.m.001","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A Philippine student hears a kulintang through the air. What carries the sound?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"No matter or energy","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.1.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"A material medium"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Empty space alone","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.1.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Light alone","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.1.2"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.m.002","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A kulintang note sounds higher than another note. Which wave property is greater for the higher note?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Only loudness","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.2.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Only source size","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.2.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Frequency"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Only amplitude","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.2.1"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.m.003","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"medium","type":"mcq","prompt":"A Philippine coastal wave rises farther above its rest level. Which wave property is larger?","answer":"choice-3","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Frequency only","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.3.1"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Wavelength","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.3.2"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Period only","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.3.3"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Amplitude"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.m.004","deckId":"physics.waves",