perty to its meaning.","answer":{"Amplitude":"Maximum displacement from rest","Wavelength":"Spacing between matching points","Frequency":"Cycles per second"}},{"id":"physics.waves.h.001","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"hard","type":"calc","prompt":"A Philippine coastal wave model has wavelength 3 m and frequency 2 Hz. What is its speed?","answer":"6","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.waves.h.002","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"hard","type":"calc","prompt":"A kulintang sound wave has speed 340 m/s and frequency 680 Hz. What is its wavelength?","answer":"0.5","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.waves.h.003","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"hard","type":"calc","prompt":"A Cebu student hears an echo after 2 s. Sound speed is 340 m/s. How far away is the reflecting wall?","answer":"340","tolerance":0.001},{"id":"physics.waves.h.004","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"Three successive crests lie at 0 m, 2 m and 4 m. What property is the 2 m spacing?","answer":"choice-1","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Loudness","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.4.3"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Wavelength"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Amplitude","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.4.1"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Frequency","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.4.2"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.h.005","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A sensor counts 120 complete cycles in 2 seconds. Which quantity is found by dividing cycles by time?","answer":"choice-2","options":[{"id":"choice-0","text":"Amplitude","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.5.2"},{"id":"choice-1","text":"Wave speed only","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.5.3"},{"id":"choice-2","text":"Frequency"},{"id":"choice-3","text":"Wavelength","misconception":"physics.waves.mixup.5.1"}]},{"id":"physics.waves.h.006","deckId":"physics.waves","level":"hard","type":"mcq","prompt":"A ripple has frequency 4 Hz and wavelength 2 m. Which relation yields its speed of 8 m/s?","answer":"ch